# The parent enclosure/.gitignore excludes *.stl as build output. For this
# design the exported meshes ARE committed, so the folder is self-contained:
# the sliceable files sit beside the source that produced them and can be
# downloaded without needing OpenSCAD installed.
#
# They are still generated, not authored. If you change the .scad, re-export
# and commit both together, or the mesh silently stops matching the source.
!*.stl
# The two-colour cover projects are committed like the meshes (make-cover-3mf.py).
!antenna_mount_twin_cover_*_twotone.3mf
# And the back plate's, its charger label in a second colour (2026-10-31).
!back_plate_twotone.3mf
# And the stand's, the easiest way to print it (make-3mf.py). It was ignored
# until 2026-10-29, so no clone had it.
!kitten-stand-twotone.3mf
